  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since the minor axis is variable, hence&nbsp;<math><mi>e</mi></math> is a variable quantity</p><p>Therefore the equation of the tangent to the ellipse can be written as <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />This line passes through the fixed point&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> (where <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p><p>Hence, distance fro the centre of the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
